// commands.zidl — Zhaozhou command ABI, single source of truth (charter 19/29-5).
//
// Grammar: EBNF in P5 recon (RUN-20260814-1852-wave1-abi-capture FINDINGS 1.2),
// normatively restated in spec/capture_format.md 1. Two ratified extensions
// over that EBNF (both documented there):
//   * command status keyword: `command <name> <opcode> implemented|reserved`
//     — implemented commands are executed by the decoder/shell; reserved
//     commands have a FROZEN wire layout but no execution semantics yet
//     (their records still validate structurally). Since ABI v2 (wave 2)
//     this includes debug-umbrella opcodes (never game-facing; the header
//     flags-bit0 rule is unchanged).
//   * `enum` entries may carry a trailing doc comment via `//` (lexical).
//
// Fixed-point fields reference spec/qformats.md (W3): `fx16` is a Q16.16
// value carried in a 4-byte (int32) container — 16 fractional bits, 16
// integer bits, little-endian on the wire. All other Q formats live there.
//
// Opcode ranges (plan 1.E / P5 1.2, table-derived):
//   0x0000-0x00FF  frame control, views, presentation
//   0x0200-0x02FF  terrain / surface (semantic, reserved in Phase 1)
//   0x0300-0x03FF  forms / populations / procedural (reserved in Phase 1)
//   0x0400-0x04FF  audio (reserved in Phase 1)
//   0xF000-0xF0FF  bootstrap/debug umbrella — never game-facing; any frame
//                  containing one of these opcodes MUST set frame header
//                  flags bit0 contains_debug_commands (ZH_ABI_DEBUG_FLAG_REQUIRED)
//
// This file is the ABI. Generated C++/TS/SV byte-identity is enforced by
// tools/abi-gen goldens; editing layout here requires regenerating
// (`npm run abi:gen`) and re-committing every generated artifact.
//
// Wave 3 (ABI v2 content, D7 promotions — run RUN-20260815-0544): the six
// Phase-3 software-console commands are promoted reserved->implemented
// (TerrainField, SurfaceStamp, DrawForm, DrawPopulation, DrawProcedural,
// EmitAudioEvent). VERSION DECISION: `abi version` STAYS 2. The frozen rule
// (spec/capture_format.md 1.2) is "opcodes, field sets and sizes never
// change; additive change = new opcode"; promotions change execution
// semantics only, and the two payload reinterpretations below (forge_kind,
// radius/ring_width) reuse never-executed reserved pad bytes at unchanged
// offsets and sizes — the same-bytes precedent the v2 `u8 mode` ->
// `video_mode` conversion set. A bump would invalidate every committed
// wave-2 capture (their frame headers pin abi_version 2) without buying a
// single compat guarantee. Promotions are recorded in capture_format.md
// 1.2/1.3 [w3] rows.
//
// ABI v3 (2026-08-17, lighting & pose consolidation wave, run
// RUN-20260816-0046): SetEnvironment 0x0311 reserved (spec/sky_and_beams.md
// 4a — the sky extension range's first allocation, under that file's v1.2
// version bump), plus the rgb565 struct and fog_mode enum it introduces.
// VERSION DECISION: this change DOES bump `abi version` 2 -> 3 — a new
// opcode is a wire change (the frozen rule: "additive change = new opcode";
// a v2 decoder reports ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE on 0x0311, so the generation
// must be distinguishable at frame validation). Committed wave-2 captures
// pin abi_version 2 and remain valid historical evidence; a v3 replay
// refuses them by design. The same wave's QFMT_VERSION 1 -> 2 (qformats 7.6,
// amendment C1) did NOT bump the version — a numeric-law constant change
// moves no opcode, field set, or size, and leaves the frame wire untouched.

// ABI v4 (2026-09-26, the frame admission plan, run
// RUN-20260919-1656-gaps-to-zero, packet SEALPLAN): SealFramePlan 0x0003
// implemented -- the per-view pre-frame allocation/admission plan that owner
// vacation directive 2026-09-23 section 5 commissions, and the command field
// that directive PRE-AUTHORISES: the architect "is not required to duplicate a
// large policy engine merely to avoid adding a command or mailbox field" and
// must "authorize the necessary generated command, publication or service
// transport and connect its real producer and consumer."
//
// VERSION DECISION: this change DOES bump `abi version` 3 -> 4. A new opcode
// is a wire change under the frozen rule ("additive change = new opcode"); a
// v3 decoder reports ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE on 0x0003, so the generation must
// be distinguishable at frame validation. This is the same reasoning the v3
// bump recorded for SetEnvironment 0x0311, applied to an opcode that is
// implemented rather than reserved.
//
// WHY A COMMAND AND NOT A GROWN RECORD. The plan is a whole frame's admission
// agreement and it is SEALED: it is validated once, latched once, and may not
// be renegotiated (directive section 5, "Do not renegotiate a sealed frame").
// A record of its own can arrive, be refused, and be re-offered without
// disturbing BeginFrame's meaning -- and growing BeginFrame would have moved a
// layout every committed capture depends on, for a payload that is not frame
// identity.
//
// WHO CONSUMES IT: `zhao_cmd_exec` decodes and stages it;
// `zhao_measure_sealplan` validates it against every capacity in its own unit
// and against R7's giant reservation, and REFUSES it before the seal if it
// does not fit; `zhao_geom_paramarena` latches the validated numbers as its
// frame quota. The field is READ, not merely carried -- which `npm run
// abi:check` cannot tell you, because it is a drift gate and goes green on a
// field nothing reads.

abi zhao {
  version 4
  endian little
  command_alignment 16
  opcode_width u16
}

// Frame-slot bound (plan 1.E): provisional until Phase 2 measurements;
// every validator bound-checks against this constant, never a magic number.
const u32 FRAME_SLOT_BYTES = 1048576;

// Numeric-law version (spec/qformats.md §13): travels with the ABI so capture
// replay can refuse mismatched numerics. Bump on any frozen Q-format change.
// = 2 since the lighting & pose consolidation wave (RUN-20260816-0046):
// amendment C1 froze the quat16 lane (qformats §7.6). The `abi version`
// itself stays 2 for this bump — a numeric-law constant change is not a
// command-surface change (no opcode, field set, or size moved).
//
// = 3 since ruling R3, PARTICLE128 V1 NUMERIC LAW
// (reports/OWNER-RULINGS-BUILDABILITY-20260902.md): "PARTICLE_FORMAT_VERSION
// = 1; bump QFMT_VERSION 2 -> 3 on commit."
//
// THE BUMP LANDED IN ONE GENERATOR AND NOT THE OTHER. `tools/fixgen` emitted 3
// into zref_tables.hpp and compiler/src/generated/tables.ts, while this file
// still said 2 and carried it into zhao_abi.h, zhao_abi_pkg.sv and
// compiler/src/generated/abi.ts. A capture-visible numeric law disagreed with
// itself across the hardware/software boundary for a day, which is exactly the
// class of skew this constant exists to catch. The `abi version` still does
// not move: no opcode, field set or size changed.
const u16 QFMT_VERSION = 3;

// The .zpak resource kind whose bytes belong to the TWOD sampler's on-chip page
// store rather than to local SDRAM (spec/cartridge.md 3 and 4f, allocated under
// the completion ruling of 2026-09-22 item 3 from the registry's own reserved
// range). It lives HERE, in the ABI, because THREE things have to agree about
// it and they are generated from three different templates: the packer that
// stamps `kind` into a PublishResource, `zhao_cmd_exec`'s fork at the pending
// upload queue's drain, and the reference model. A number written out three
// times is a number that can disagree with itself, which is exactly what the
// QFMT_VERSION 2/3 skew above was.
const u8 RESOURCE_KIND_TWOD_PAGE = 15;

// Error codes — generated verbatim into C++/TS/SV and shared by the frame
// validator (spec/capture_format.md 4.2), the .zcap tools, and the stub RTL.
// Order matters: it is the fail-safe validation order of capture_format.md.
// Values 0-11 are the P5 3.3 set; 12-14 are wave-1 ratifications (1.E).
enum zhao_abi_error : u32 {
  ZH_ABI_OK = 0;                     // frame accepted
  ZH_ABI_BAD_MAGIC = 1;              // frame magic mismatch
  ZH_ABI_BAD_ABI_VERSION = 2;        // abi_version != generated ABI version
  ZH_ABI_RESERVED_FLAG = 3;          // undefined flag bit set (frame or record)
  ZH_ABI_BAD_LENGTH = 4;             // lengths misaligned / out of bounds
  ZH_ABI_BAD_HEADER_CRC = 5;         // header_crc32c mismatch
  ZH_ABI_BAD_PAYLOAD_CRC = 6;        // payload_crc32c mismatch
  ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE = 7;         // opcode not in the generated table
  ZH_ABI_RESERVED_FIELD = 8;         // reserved/pad byte nonzero on the wire
  ZH_ABI_BAD_VALUE = 9;              // enum/bitfield out of range
                                     // (first user: SetView depth_profile == 3)
  ZH_ABI_STALE_HANDLE = 10;          // handle generation mismatch (none in v1)
  ZH_ABI_TRUNCATED = 11;             // records end before command_bytes
  ZH_ABI_DEBUG_FLAG_REQUIRED = 12;   // 0xF00n opcode without header flags bit0
  ZH_ABI_COUNT_MISMATCH = 13;        // records walked != command_count
  ZH_ABI_UNIMPLEMENTED_COMMAND = 14; // executor-level: reserved opcode used
}

// ---- value enums (ABI v2, wave 2) -------------------------------------------

// Presentation/video mode — the ONE mode selector machine-wide (plan D6).
// Wire-identical with the Phase-1 `u8 mode` of SetPresentationContract and
// the .zcap FRAMEBUFFER_EXPECTED `mode` byte; RTL latches it only at frame
// start (vblank) — effective next frame, never mid-frame (spec/video_rules.md).
enum video_mode : u8 {
  VIDEO_Z60 = 0;    // 384x240, canvas 184,320 B RGB565
  VIDEO_STORM = 1;  // 320x240, canvas 153,600 B RGB565
  VIDEO_DUO = 2;   // 512x240 (2 x 256x192); STORES 196,608 B (0x30000,
                   // two packed view blocks — video_rules.md 1/3.1: the
                   // 0x3C000 slot ALLOCATION and the 245,760-B DISPLAYED
                   // stream are different numbers; DebugFrameBlit.byte_len
                   // carries the 196,608 occupancy)
}

// [w3/D7] Primitive Forge kind for DrawProcedural. Member 0 is deliberately
// the wave-3 island form: the byte reused by this enum was a mandatory-zero
// pad in v2, so ABI-v2-era records (zero there) remain valid and now read as
// the one implemented kind. New kinds are additive members (values ascend);
// a value outside the member set is ZH_ABI_BAD_VALUE (rule 1.1-8).
// THE FIVE MEMBERS BELOW WERE ADDED BY OWNER RULING R108 (2026-09-20), which
// applies this file's own additive law rather than creating one: "forge_kind
// has exactly one member while FORGE.PRIM has six families, so the ABI cannot
// name five of them ... No `abi_version` bump is implied." The families are
// CLOSED at six by owner ruling 2026-08-31 6.5, restated by R11 -- ribbon,
// radial fan/ring, tube, radial shell, billboard sheet, terrain cliff/skirt --
// and the four deleted candidates (shard burst, chain, spline wall, low cone)
// are NOT reserved for later; see design/contracts/FORGE.PRIM.md:7-14.
//
// !! THIS ENUM IS NOT `zhao_forge_prim`'s `j_family_i` ENCODING. DO NOT WIRE
// !! ONE TO THE OTHER. They are two numberings of the same six families and
// !! they DISAGREE, because member 0 here is frozen by the v2 pad-byte
// !! precedent above and cannot be renumbered to match. The silicon's order is
// !! `zhao_forge_prim.sv:87-92` (FAM_RIBBON=0 .. FAM_CLIFF=5), mirrored by
// !! `zref::forge::Family` (reference/include/zref/zref_forge.hpp:35-42) and by
// !! tests/forge/forge_prim_directed.cpp:47. The translation is exact and it is
// !! a ROTATION, not an identity:
// !!
// !!     forge_kind          value   <->  FAM_* (zhao_forge_prim.sv)
// !!     FORGE_HEIGHTFIELD_PATCH 0    <->  FAM_CLIFF      5
// !!     FORGE_RIBBON            1    <->  FAM_RIBBON     0
// !!     FORGE_RADIAL_FAN        2    <->  FAM_FAN        1
// !!     FORGE_TUBE              3    <->  FAM_TUBE       2
// !!     FORGE_RADIAL_SHELL      4    <->  FAM_SHELL      3
// !!     FORGE_BILLBOARD_SHEET   5    <->  FAM_BILLBOARD  4
// !!
// !! i.e. forge_kind = (FAM_* + 1) mod 6. No RTL consumes `forge_kind` today,
// !! so the two numberings have never had to meet; whoever first wires
// !! DrawProcedural to a FORGE.PRIM job owns this conversion and owes it a
// !! directed check. A straight-through assignment is silently wrong for all
// !! six values.
//
// MEMBER 0 IS THE `terrain cliff / skirt` FAMILY under this ruling -- that is
// what makes R108's arithmetic (six families, one member, five owed) come out,
// and member 0's own comment already says "terrain skirt/ground". It is
// recorded here because it is an INFERENCE from R108's count and not a
// sentence the owner wrote; FINDINGS-zidl.md carries it as an owner question.
// If it is instead a seventh, software-only island form, then the cliff/skirt
// family is still unnamed and a sixth member appends at 6 under this same
// additive law -- no renumber, and nothing below changes.
//
// Four of the six families have NO EVALUATOR (fan, tube, shell, billboard):
// FORGE.PRIM.EVAL serves the ribbon family only, and cliff is FORGE.CLIFF's
// two unruled rivals (R109). Naming a family here does not implement it.
enum forge_kind : u8 {
  FORGE_HEIGHTFIELD_PATCH = 0;  // authored heightfield patch projected as
                                // terrain skirt/ground — the Wound Lab island
  FORGE_RIBBON = 1;             // ribbon (FAM_RIBBON) — the only family with a
                                // position evaluator (FORGE.PRIM.EVAL)
  FORGE_RADIAL_FAN = 2;         // radial fan / ring (FAM_FAN) — no evaluator
  FORGE_TUBE = 3;               // tube (FAM_TUBE) — no evaluator
  FORGE_RADIAL_SHELL = 4;       // radial shell (FAM_SHELL) — no evaluator
  FORGE_BILLBOARD_SHEET = 5;    // billboard sheet (FAM_BILLBOARD) — no evaluator
}

// [v3, sky_and_beams v1.2] Fog mode (law: qformats.md 8; sky_and_beams 4a).
// Members ascend additively; the deferred exponential form appends, never
// renumbers (the forge_kind member-0 precedent).
enum fog_mode : u8 {
  FOG_OFF = 0;
  FOG_LINEAR = 1;
}

// [v3, GEOM.WARP decision W06] How `DrawWarpedForm 0x0304` supplies the Warp
// program's four attribute lanes a0..a3 (spec/form/field-ir.md 7.1, canonical
// input lanes 6..9).
//
// IT IS AN ENUM AND NOT THE DIRECTIVE'S `u8`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT.
// reports/Zhaozhou_GEOM_WARP_Architecture_2026-09-20.txt 6.3 requires that
// "other values [are] refused" and, one line further down, that "payload
// validation is generated/centralized with the decoder". An enum field is
// exactly that mechanism already built: `tools/abi-gen/src/oracle.ts` emits a
// payload-relative {offset, size, valid values} row for every enum field and
// the decoder answers ZH_ABI_BAD_VALUE on anything else (capture_format.md 3.2
// step 7, active since ABI v2). Declaring it `u8` would have left 6.3's refusal
// to a hand-written check in whichever consumer remembered to write one --
// which is the private-switch failure 6.4 names by hand. The WIRE IS
// IDENTICAL: an enum rides its backing prim, so this is one byte at payload
// offset 60 either way and W04's 80-byte payload is unchanged.
//
// Members ascend additively (the forge_kind member-0 precedent). A third
// attribute source appends at 2; it never renumbers these two.
enum warp_attribute_mode : u8 {
  // Four inline constant words in the record, the same for every vertex of the
  // draw. `warp_attributes` MUST be 0 (6.3).
  WARP_ATTR_INLINE4 = 0;
  // Four per-vertex words from the resident WARP_ATTRIBUTES resource named by
  // `warp_attributes`. The four inline words MUST be zero (6.3) -- unused
  // ambiguous content is refused rather than ignored.
  WARP_ATTR_STREAM4 = 1;
}

// ---- composed fixed-point containers (element = fx16, Q16.16, spec/qformats.md)

// Axis-aligned footprint in world units.
struct rectfx {
  fx16 x0;
  fx16 y0;
  fx16 x1;
  fx16 y1;
}

// Affine 2D transform: translation then row-major 2x2.
struct transform2fx {
  fx16 tx;
  fx16 ty;
  fx16 r00;
  fx16 r01;
  fx16 r10;
  fx16 r11;
}

// Row-major 4x4 view-projection matrix.
struct mat4fx {
  fx16 m00;
  fx16 m01;
  fx16 m02;
  fx16 m03;
  fx16 m10;
  fx16 m11;
  fx16 m12;
  fx16 m13;
  fx16 m20;
  fx16 m21;
  fx16 m22;
  fx16 m23;
  fx16 m30;
  fx16 m31;
  fx16 m32;
  fx16 m33;
}

// [v3, sky_and_beams v1.2] Packed RGB565 colour (rrrrrggggggbbbbbb) — the
// resolve wire format (qformats.md 2 colour8: "RGB565 at resolve");
// expansion law: stars_and_flares.md 2 bit replication.
struct rgb565 {
  u16 bits;
}

// ---- controller (plan D5): the canonical pad snapshot ------------------------
//
// ONE definition machine-wide: the .zcap CONTROLLER_SNAPSHOT (0x0004) entry
// IS this struct; abi-gen emits it into C++/TS/SV and fpga/rtl/common/
// zhao_pkg.sv re-exports the generated SV type.
//
// Size reconciliation (plan D5 said "24 B, 4-aligned"; the shipped .zcap
// 0x0004 layout is 20 B): the .zidl grammar (capture_format.md 1.1 rule 3)
// caps element alignment at 4 — a 4-byte `buttons` inside every array
// element requires a stride divisible by 4. The declared fields of the
// shipped section sum to 18 B; one explicit 4-byte reserved word closes the
// struct at exactly 20 B, already 4-aligned. 24 B would NOT be
// wire-compatible with the shipped 0x0004 section, and the grammar forbids
// the hidden 2-4 tail bytes a 24-B layout would need. DECISION: 20 B
// (u32 rsv), array stride 20. Law: spec/input_rules.md.
struct PadFrame {
  u8 pad_index;   // 0-3 (four slots, charter 17)
  u8 flags;       // bit0 = pad_present; bits 1-7 reserved 0
  u16 sequence;   // per-pad monotonic snapshot sequence
  u32 buttons;    // 32 digital bits (bit i = button i, active high)
  i16 lx;         // left stick X,  signed, center 0
  i16 ly;         // left stick Y,  signed, center 0, positive = down
  i16 rx;         // right stick X, signed, center 0
  i16 ry;         // right stick Y, signed, center 0, positive = down
  u32 rsv;        // reserved, must be 0 (closes the struct at 20 B / stride 4)
}

// ---- MATERIAL_SET record (frozen 2026-09-05, roadmap G2-A) -----------------
//
// MATERIAL.RESOLVE.md said "the record layout inside MATERIAL_SET is still not
// frozen -- the draft above is a draft, and the ABI generator owns the emitted
// constants". Owner ruling D-2 made freezing the three generic families step 2
// of the implementation order, and D-2 allocated the kinds:
//   10 TEXTURE_PAGE (0x000E) | 11 MATERIAL_SET (0x000F) | 12 MESH_STREAM (0x0010)
//
// So this is the freeze, and it lives here because the generator owns the
// constants -- a record hand-written into zhao_abi.h would be a second source
// of truth for a layout the RTL, the packer and the reference all read.
//
// SHAPE. The draft used sub-byte widths (u2 sample_count, u3 recipe, u4
// tmu_mode ...). The .zidl grammar is whole-byte, so the packing is explicit
// and documented per field rather than implied by a bitfield the three
// backends would each lay out their own way. 32 bytes exactly: it is the same
// size as a command record, it is 4-aligned for array use, and a material
// table is indexed by material_id so a power-of-two stride is a shift.
//
// It resolves to EXACTLY what FRAGROB's input packet needs, which is the whole
// point -- the contract's words: "a material record resolves to exactly what
// FRAGROB's input packet needs, so the two cannot drift".
//
// `tmu_mode` -- RATIFIED BY R77 (2026-09-20), AND THIS COMMENT USED TO CONTRADICT
// THE SILICON. It read "bits 0-3 tmu_mode (nearest/bilinear/CLUT/direct)", which
// is not a value list but reads exactly like one, and so puts CLUT at 2. The
// composed island has shipped with the opposite numbering since it was written:
// `zhao_texture_island_v3_top.sv:222-225` declares `CLS_CLUT = 2'd0`,
// `CLS_NEAR = 2'd1`, `CLS_BIL = 2'd2`, `CLS_ERR = 2'd3`. R77 ratifies the
// island's constants -- "it is DERIVED rather than chosen ... the constant that
// was already there" -- so the ABI is what moved, not the hardware.
//
// The cost of leaving it was specific, which is why R77 called this the real
// reason that pays for the capture regeneration: anyone implementing from the
// ABI spec would have got CLUT wrong, and `witness_mismatch_o` exists to
// difference two INDEPENDENT sources -- it would have been differencing two
// copies of the same mistake and reading zero. A detector fed a shared error
// is the failure mode CLAUDE.md is built around.
//
// Value 3 is reserved on the wire: the island spends it on CLS_ERR, its refusal
// class, which is a response the fabric raises and never a mode a command asks
// for.
struct MaterialSample {
  u16 binding_slot;        // texture binding this sample reads
  u8  binding_generation;  // D-3 residency generation, low 8 bits
  u8  modes;               // bits 0-3 tmu_mode: 0 CLUT, 1 NEAREST, 2 BILINEAR,
                           //   3 reserved (R77 -- values, NOT a reading order)
                           // bits 4-5 wrap (0 repeat, 1 clamp, 2 mirror, 3 rsv)
                           // bits 6-7 mip_policy
}

struct MaterialRecord {
  u8  control;        // bits 0-1 sample_count (0..3, the ruling limit)
                      // bits 2-4 recipe (the six ratified combiner recipes)
                      // bits 5-7 reserved, must be 0
  u8  recipe_weight;  // unit8; used by LERP only (value = raw/256)
  u16 flags;          // bit0 toon, bit1 ink, bit2 alpha_test; 3-15 reserved 0
  MaterialSample sample0;
  MaterialSample sample1;
  MaterialSample sample2;
  u32 palette_base;   // CLUT modes only; 0 when no sample is a CLUT mode
  u32 raster_state;   // R28: bits 2-31 carried unchanged to the triangle
                      // descriptor's raster_state[31:2] (no v1 consumer: 0);
                      // bits 0-1 reserved 0 -- the cull mode is the DRAW's
                      // (DrawForm flags[3:2]). Model: zref::raster_state.
  u32 fragment_state; // THE FRAGMENT PIPELINE'S 32-BIT STATE WORD, v1 schema
                      // (zhao_render_texture_pkg::zhao_fragment_state_v1_t,
                      // mirror zref::FragmentPipeline::State). Bit for bit the
                      // word zhao_raster_fragment.sv has always decoded:
                      //   [0] Z_TEST_EN      [1] Z_WRITE_DIS  [2] Z_FORCE_FAR
                      //   [4:3] BLEND        [5] SHADE_MOD    [6] ALPHA_MOD
                      //   [7] ATEST_EN       [15:8] ATEST_REF
                      //   [17:16] STEN_FUNC  [19:18] STEN_OP
                      //   [20] TAG_WRITE_DIS [21] TAG_FROM_TEXEL
                      //   [23:22] TAG_CHANNEL [31:24] STEN_MASK
                      // MUST BE 0 unless fragment_decl bit0 is set -- see the
                      // contradiction rule below.
                      // NOT R28's raster_state: that word is the TRIANGLE
                      // DESCRIPTOR's draw-state sideband with its own cull
                      // field, four bytes up. Same width, same English name,
                      // different layouts, different consumers, and the owner
                      // directive names confusing them as a trap by itself.
                      // zref_raster_state.hpp's header says the same.
  u32 fragment_decl;  // bit0     fragment_declared -- THE EXPLICIT SELECTOR
                      // bits 1-7 reserved, must be 0
                      // bits 8-15  effect_tag        (u8)
                      // bits 16-23 stencil_reference (u8)
                      // bits 24-31 reserved, must be 0 (closes at 32 B)
}

// ---- THE FRAGMENT PROFILE, allocated 2026-09-25 (FRAGSTATE) ----------------
// Owner vacation directive of 2026-09-23 section 3: "Expose the missing
// reference/mask/state through real material/draw/primitive producers, using
// validated versioned extensions or a new opcode where needed."
//
// SUPERSEDES the two words' previous declaration -- `u32 rsv0; u32 rsv1;
// // reserved, must be 0`. Nothing else about MaterialRecord moves.
//
// VERSION: UNCHANGED at 3, and no opcode is allocated. This is a same-bytes
// reinterpretation of two MANDATORY-ZERO words at unchanged offsets (24 and 28)
// and unchanged sizes, which is the ratified pattern -- the DrawProcedural
// frame_tick/material_id allocation and SetView's depth_profile are the
// precedents, and capture_format.md 1.3's "opcode, field set and sizes never
// change" is honoured because none of the three does.
//
// ZERO KEEPS ITS MEANING, which is the whole reason these two words were chosen
// over any other carrier. Both were already refused-if-nonzero by BOTH mirrors
// (zref::material_resolve's record_legal and zhao_material_resolve.sv's
// record_ok_f), so every committed capture has them zero, and zero now decodes
// to "this material declares no fragment profile" -- under which the primitive
// producer's own door declaration stands exactly as it did before this line was
// written. No existing capture changes by one pixel.
//
// THE SELECTOR IS EXPLICIT AND THE CONTRADICTION IS REFUSED. The directive says
// "profile selection is explicit, not inferred from whether a port happens to be
// zero", and that is load-bearing here rather than decorative: the all-zero
// state word IS a legal and meaningful profile -- frag_profile_opaque_geometry(),
// the plain opaque write -- so "is the word zero?" cannot be the question.
// fragment_decl bit0 answers it. And a record with bit0 CLEAR but a non-zero
// fragment_state, or a non-zero effect_tag or stencil_reference, is a
// CONTRADICTORY DECLARATION: it is REFUSED whole and counted, never masked.
// That is SetPost.flags's discipline ("CMD.EXEC drops the record and counts it,
// it never masks a bit it does not know") rather than compose()'s silent mask,
// and it catches the one mistake this shape invites -- a producer that fills the
// state and forgets the flag, whose material would otherwise be drawn opaque
// with no diagnostic.
//
// WHY THE MATERIAL AND NOT THE DRAW. DrawForm.flags has 12 unassigned bits and
// they are NOT enforced zero: the committed golden cmd_draw_form.bin's own
// sample sets flags = 0xB338, i.e. bits 4,5,8,9,12,13 and 15. Claiming one would
// change the meaning of bytes existing captures already carry, which is the one
// thing the frozen-opcode rule forbids. Measured, not assumed.
//
// WHY NOT MaterialRecord.raster_state[31:2], which also has 30 spare bits: that
// word is R28's TRIANGLE DESCRIPTOR state, and the directive explicitly names
// confusing the two as a trap. It is also not actually carried -- both mirrors
// substitute a named constant for it (zref_drawjob.hpp's kV1MaterialRaster = 0
// and zhao_geom_drawjob.sv's V1_MATERIAL_RASTER_C = 30'd0) -- so plumbing the
// fragment profile through it would have been routing a live value down a
// channel whose current content is an invented zero. Separate identity, separate
// word.
//
// WHY A WHOLE 32-BIT WORD rather than a small profile index. The directive
// requires "stencil reference and mask are explicit u8 values", and the MASK is
// a field of this very word ([31:24] STEN_MASK) -- it is not a separate quantity
// and must never become a second port to the same silicon. An index into a table
// of eight named recipes could not express a mask, an ATEST_REF or a stencil
// function at all. The named profiles in zhao_render_texture_pkg.sv are how a
// producer CONSTRUCTS this word conveniently; they are not a narrower channel it
// has to squeeze through.

// ---- frame control ---------------------------------------------------------

command Nop 0x0000 implemented {
  // decoder test vehicle; record = bare 16-byte command header
}

command BeginFrame 0x0001 implemented {
  u32 frame_id;
  u32 resource_epoch;
  u32 flags;
  u32 deadline_cycles;
}

// ---- THE FRAME ADMISSION PLAN (owner vacation directive section 5) --------
//
// THE SEAL NAMES FOUR UNITS AND THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. The directive:
// "The seal names frame/view/resource generation, capacities, vertex/triangle/
// reference/chunk limits, and the designated giant's reservation. Keep those
// units distinct." And: "Do not confuse references with chunks or assume a
// reference budget pays for every other structure."
//
//   plan_verts   VERTICES         arena vertex slots
//   plan_tris    TRIANGLES        arena triangle descriptors
//   plan_chunks  CHUNKS           arena chunk payload units
//   plan_refs    TILE REFERENCES  binner reference RAM
//   giant_refs   TILE REFERENCES  the guaranteed giant's reservation
//
// THE FOUR ORDINARY BUDGETS ARE ORDINARY-ONLY. The giant's reservation is
// subtracted from capacity BEFORE the ordinary demand is checked against what
// remains -- "reserve ... before ordinary kMesh allocation" is an allocation-
// ORDER statement and the plan is where that order is applied. A plan whose
// ordinary demand plus the reservation exceeds a capacity is REFUSED before
// the seal, in that unit, naming that unit.
//
// `giant_refs` MUST BE 32,768 EXACTLY when `flags` bit 0 is set, and MUST BE
// ZERO when it is clear. It is carried on the wire rather than implied so the
// plan the software computed and the reservation the hardware enforces are the
// same statement and can be differenced; a reservation that only exists in
// hardware cannot be checked against the budget the planner actually spent.
// The hardware refuses any other value: the delegation does not cover shrinking
// the guaranteed giant, so a trimmed reservation is an ILLEGAL plan and not a
// smaller one. ceil(32768/14) = 2,341 CHUNKS is derived in hardware and is NOT
// a wire field -- deriving it twice is how the 14x confusion gets a second
// chance.
//
// THE ABSENT GIANT IS AN EXPLICIT DECLARATION. "A frame explicitly containing
// no guaranteed giant may release that reservation BEFORE sealing." `flags`
// bit 0 clear is that declaration and the full capacity becomes available.
//
// `giant_instance` is the designated giant's STABLE INSTANCE IDENTITY, in the
// same space as a draw record's header `source_id`. The hardware selects by
// declared priority (`semantic_weight`) and breaks ties on this identity; the
// field is what the frame's own draw stream is CHECKED AGAINST at frame end,
// not a hint. It is ignored when bit 0 is clear.
//
// GENERATIONS. `resource_gen` and `view_gen` are the generations the plan was
// computed against; a plan whose generations do not match the console's live
// values is refused, because a plan priced against a resource set that has
// since been replaced is a plan for a different frame. The FRAME generation is
// not a wire field: it is stamped by the hardware at the seal, for the same
// reason `zhao_geom_paramarena` refuses to let a caller supply it -- a
// caller-supplied generation lets a carried-over record keep last frame's
// stamp, which is the one thing the field exists to make detectable.
command SealFramePlan 0x0003 implemented {
  u8  view_id;         // which view this plan admits
  u8  flags;           // bit0 giant_present; bits 7:1 reserved, MUST BE ZERO
  u16 resource_gen;    // resource generation the plan was priced against
  u16 view_gen;        // view generation the plan was priced against
  u16 giant_instance;  // stable instance identity of the designated giant
  u32 plan_verts;      // VERTICES,        ordinary
  u32 plan_tris;       // TRIANGLES,       ordinary
  u32 plan_chunks;     // CHUNKS,          ordinary
  u32 plan_refs;       // TILE REFERENCES, ordinary
  u32 giant_refs;      // TILE REFERENCES, the reservation (32768 or 0)
  pad[4];
}

command EndFrame 0x0002 implemented {
  u32 completion_flags;
  u32 expected_crc_valid;
  u32 expected_framebuffer_crc;
  pad[4];
}

// ---- views / presentation --------------------------------------------------

// SETVIEW FLAGS, owner ruling 2026-08-31 section 1 (FROZEN CONSOLE LAW).
//
//   bits [1:0]  depth_profile      00 WORLD_LONG      1.0  m .. 16384 m
//                                  01 WORLD_STANDARD  0.5  m ..  8192 m
//                                  10 CLOSE           0.25 m ..  2048 m
//                                  11 RESERVED -- REFUSED, ZH_ABI_BAD_VALUE
//   bits [15:2] UNASSIGNED -- available for future view flags. NOT required
//               to be zero: the ruling assigns [1:0] and says nothing about
//               the rest, and `zhao_sample_set_view()` already carries 0x8261.
//
// WIRE-IDENTICAL. `flags` already existed and was undefined; this assigns
// meaning to two of its bits and changes no offset, size or CRC. That is why
// the ruling chose it over a new opcode.
//
// ZERO KEEPS ITS MEANING. 00 is WORLD_LONG, so an existing zero-filled capture
// still decodes to the profile it was recorded under. Had CLOSE been 00, every
// archived capture would have silently changed depth.
//
// The profile travels WITH the view, is recorded in captures and is reproduced
// in replay. Games do not upload near/far values -- scale and shift stay
// generated from the frozen reciprocal law (spec/qformats.md 8). A fourth
// profile needs new evidence, a new proof and an explicit ABI ruling; it may
// not be smuggled in as custom numbers, which is what 11 being REFUSED rather
// than aliased protects.
// THE EYE, ruling R63 of reports/OWNER-RULINGS-20260919-EVENING.md.
//
// `view_projection` is the FUSED matrix. A world-space camera POSITION cannot
// be recovered from it without a 4x4 inverse that nothing in this console
// ratifies, and TERRAIN.LOD's screen-space-error law needs the eye in world
// units to measure distance to a subpatch centre. So the eye travels on the
// wire beside the matrix that was built from it, as ONE record under ONE
// commit -- the same reason `flags[1:0]` rides here rather than arriving
// separately.
//
// UNITS: fx16 Q16.16 world metres, the same container and the same frame as
// `SurfaceStamp.transform` translations and TERRAIN.PATCH's world origins.
// ORDER: eye[0]=x, eye[1]=y, eye[2]=z.
//
// ZERO IS LEGAL AND MEANS THE ORIGIN. A console that never writes an eye puts
// every camera at (0,0,0), which is a defensible picture and not a fault; the
// consumer's own `cam*_en_i` decides whether a view participates at all. This
// is the same zero-keeps-its-meaning property the depth profile has, and it is
// why no "eye present" flag bit is spent.
//
// This GROWS the record from 96 to 112 bytes. It is the first layout growth of
// an already-implemented command in this ABI, so: every generated output, both
// wave-2 golden capture sets and the console's own elaboration guard move with
// it, and `zhao_cmd_exec.sv`'s `ZHAO_SET_VIEW_BYTES != 96` $fatal is the thing
// that makes a half-done move impossible to ship quietly.
command SetView 0x0010 implemented {
  u8 view_id;
  u8 viewport_id;
  u16 flags;      // [1:0] depth_profile; [15:2] unassigned
  mat4fx view_projection;
  fx16 pixel_error;
  u32 geometry_tokens;
  u32 fragment_tokens;
  fx16 eye[3];    // [R63] camera position, world metres Q16.16 (x, y, z)
  pad[4];
}

command SetPresentationContract 0x0020 implemented {
  video_mode mode;  // ABI v2: was `u8 mode` — wire-identical (1 byte, same offset)
  u8 view_count;
  u16 flags;
  u32 geometry_tokens[2];
  u32 fragment_tokens[2];
  u32 shared_tokens;
  pad[8];
}

// ---- terrain / surface (semantic commands; implemented in wave 3 — D7)

// [w3] EXECUTED by the software console (zref terrain stage): applies the
// earth field .zprog named by `program` (cartridge PROGRAM page, spec/
// cartridge.md 3 kind 0) over the heightfield columns inside `footprint`,
// via the zfield interpreter (field-ir.md 1.1 — the only C++ semantics).
// Parameter-blob convention (spec/form/domains-and-effects.md 5): the earth
// params-struct lanes packed Q16.16 LE in declaration order into p0..p7
// (field-ir.md 7.1) — bytes [0, 4*lane_count) carry lanes, the rest MUST be
// zero. start_tick/duration_ticks drive the age/phase input lanes exactly.
command TerrainField 0x0200 implemented {
  handle32[program] program;
  rectfx footprint;
  u32 start_tick;
  u32 duration_ticks;
  u8 parameters[64];
  pad[4];
}

// [w3] EXECUTED by the software console (surface-sheet stage): stamps a
// circle/ring into the 64x64 surface sheet named by `brush` (SURFACE_STAMP
// is the scar response of D7). Geometry: circle of `radius` (world metres,
// fx16) at the transform translation; when `ring_width` > 0 the filled disc
// becomes an annulus [radius - ring_width, radius]. tag/strength/operation
// are the stamp-profile output vocabulary (field-ir.md 7.1 stamp record:
// tag_op semantics as u8 tag + operation, strength scaled u16).
// radius/ring_width reuse bytes that were mandatory-zero pad in v2 (same-
// bytes reinterpretation, capture_format.md 1.3 [w3]); ring stamps were
// unrepresentable before, so no v2 record changes meaning.
command SurfaceStamp 0x0210 implemented {
  handle32[brush] brush;
  handle32[patch] patch;
  u8 operation;        // stamp op: 0 = stamp, 1 = decay-accumulate (L1 uses 0)
  u8 tag;              // surface-sheet tag byte (scar family)
  u16 strength;        // 0..65535 initial/peak strength
  transform2fx transform;  // sheet placement (translation = centre)
  fx16 radius;         // [w3] circle radius, world metres
  fx16 ring_width;     // [w3] 0 = filled disc, >0 = annulus of this width
  pad[4];
}

// [v3] THE TERRAIN WORLD ABI, ruling T5 of
// reports/OWNER-RULINGS-BUILDABILITY-20260902.md, verbatim. That ruling fixes
// both opcodes and both layouts and says "opcodes confirmed by the ZIDL
// generator before commit" -- this is that commit. 0x0220 and 0x0230 were
// unallocated; the range comment at the top of this section already reserves
// 0x0200-0x02FF for terrain.
//
// RESERVED, NOT IMPLEMENTED, and the distinction is the honest one: the ABI is
// frozen and the pager behind it is built and unit-verified (TERRAIN.SEQ,
// TERRAIN.LOADQ, TERRAIN.PAGELOADER, TERRAIN.RESIDENCY, TERRAIN.PAGESTREAM,
// TERRAIN.MIPFEED), but NOTHING TURNS A COMMAND INTO A FRAME yet -- the
// composed bench plays the frame ring by hand. A game issuing one of these
// today gets ZH_ABI_UNIMPLEMENTED_COMMAND, which is a clean refusal rather
// than silence. See reports/TERRAIN-COMMAND-PIPELINE-20260907.md for what the
// executor has to do and for the four rulings it still needs.

// Epoch control for the terrain resource set. BEGIN publishes a new
// resource_epoch; END_FLUSH waits for the pager to drain; ABORT drops the
// current set. WHAT "DRAIN" MEANS IN GATES IS NOT RULED -- which counters must
// be quiet, and whether a fault during the flush aborts or holds the epoch --
// and that is listed as an open ruling rather than decided here.
command TerrainEpoch 0x0220 reserved {
  u32 epoch;                 // the resource_epoch this command establishes
  u8  op;                    // 0 = BEGIN, 1 = END_FLUSH, 2 = ABORT
  u8  flags;                 // reserved-0 in v1
  u16 reserved;              // must be 0
  // T5 calls this a HANDLE. There is no `island_table` handle class in this
  // file and adding one is a generator change plus a ruling about its
  // generation semantics, so it is a u32 here -- WIRE-IDENTICAL to a
  // handle32, differing only in what the decoder validates. Named in the
  // pipeline report as work, not left to look like a considered choice.
  u32 island_table_handle;
  u32 source_id;
}

// The whole visible+prefetch set for one frame, as ONE command. T5: "One
// SubmitTerrainSet covers the whole required+prefetch set. Do not emit one
// DrawProcedural per patch and do not overload an existing terrain field
// command."
//
// list_offset/list_bytes name a run of 32-byte patch records in the HPS
// staging arena -- the record `zref::swstream::encode_record` already
// serialises and `zref::swstream::canonical_less` already sorted. THE SEALED
// LIST IS CAPTURE DATA: replay does not rerun the HPS visibility walk, so
// nothing in hardware may re-sort or re-derive it.
//
// list_bytes must be exactly 32 * patch_count. Anything else is a malformed
// command, not a clamp.
//
// PAYLOAD BYTES 16..31 DO NOT REACH THE SCHEDULER TODAY. The shell's record
// framer captures record bytes 16..31 -- i.e. payload bytes 0..15 -- so
// resource_epoch, list_offset, list_bytes and list_crc32c arrive and
// patch_count, view_mask, flags and sequence do not. That is a command-path
// limit and not a terrain one: TerrainField 0x0200 is a 112-byte record and is
// truncated the same way. The field ORDER here is T5's and is not rearranged
// to suit the framer -- moving patch_count into the first sixteen bytes would
// be designing the ABI around a bug.
command SubmitTerrainSet 0x0230 reserved {
  u32 resource_epoch;        // must equal the live epoch or the command is refused
  u32 list_offset;           // byte offset of the patch list in the HPS staging arena
  u32 list_bytes;            // exactly 32 * patch_count
  u32 list_crc32c;           // over the whole list, checked BEFORE any load is issued
  u16 patch_count;           // T5's SEAL: TERRAIN.SEQ stops here, not at a sentinel
  u8  view_mask;             // which views this set was unioned for
  u8  flags;                 // reserved-0 in v1
  u32 sequence;              // the frame sequence this set belongs to
  u32 reserved0;             // must be 0
  u32 reserved1;             // must be 0 (closes the payload at 32 B)
}

// ---- forms / populations / procedural (implemented in wave 3 — D7)

// [w3] EXECUTED by the software renderer (marker/billboard path — the two
// wizards, marker-law lineage of the wave-2 Duo demo). The L1 draw_form emit
// lowers here (spec/form/language-semantics.md 5). `form` names a cartridge
// page (marker quad set); `transform` names the transform resource for the
// entity. Payload flags bits [w3]: b0 = billboard (face the view camera),
// b1 = screen-space size (marker law) vs world-space size; b2-3 = CULL MODE
// (owner ruling R28, provisional: 0 NONE double-sided, 1 NEG, 2 POS,
// 3 reserved and REFUSED) -- it becomes the triangle descriptor's
// raster_state[1:0], FIRST and from the draw, the rest of that word being
// the material's (MaterialRecord.raster_state[31:2]); layout in
// design/contracts/GEOM.PARAMBUF.md, model zref::raster_state. A draw that
// never set b2-3 is NONE, the behaviour every existing capture was recorded
// under. Bits 4-15 reserved 0. semantic_weight feeds the Measure policy
// (degrade order).
command DrawForm 0x0300 implemented {
  handle32[form] form;
  handle32[material_set] material_set;
  handle32[transform] transform;
  u8 viewport_mask;
  u8 semantic_weight;
  u16 flags;
}

// [w3] EXECUTED by the software renderer: point/triangle particle sprites
// from a pool's SoA state through the generated-code manifest (draw_population
// emit, spec/form/language-semantics.md 5). Payload flags bits [w3]:
// b0 = point sprites, b1 = triangle sprites (both may be set; ladder-free
// L1 chooses statically); bits 2-15 reserved 0.
command DrawPopulation 0x0301 implemented {
  handle32[population] population;
  u8 viewport_mask;
  u8 semantic_weight;
  u16 flags;
  pad[8];
}

// [w3] EXECUTED by the software renderer: Primitive Forge descriptor in
// software — the island (forge_kind FORGE_HEIGHTFIELD_PATCH projects the
// authored terrain-patch page per D7/D9-island). Parameter-blob convention:
// forge parameters do NOT travel inline; `program` names the cartridge
// terrain-patch page (spec/cartridge.md 4 kind 4) whose header carries the
// patch extents, and `transform`/`screen_error` carry placement + the
// pixels-per-error policy. forge_kind reuses a mandatory-zero v2 pad byte
// (same-bytes reinterpretation, capture_format.md 1.3 [w3]).
//
// [2026-09-22, OWNER COMPLETION RULING ITEM 2 — THE (SET HANDLE, RECORD ID)
// PAIR] The material reference is now stated, and it is TWO values:
//
//     material_set : the COMPLETE handle32[material_set] (this field)
//     material_id  : an independent u16 index within that set
//
// THE FIELD WAS `handle32[material] material` AND THE RESOURCE KIND WAS AN
// ORPHAN -- `handle32[material]` occurred exactly ONCE in this whole file, on
// this line, and nothing anywhere stated how it became `zhao_material_window`'s
// (set, id) key. The ruling settles it: "Keep the existing 32-bit material word
// intact and define it as the material-set handle." So the field is renamed to
// `material_set` and its kind to `material_set`, which is the SAME KIND AND THE
// SAME OFFSET AND WIDTH every other draw command already uses (DrawForm 0x0300,
// DrawPosedForm 0x0305, DrawWarpedForm 0x0304). NO WIRE BYTE MOVES.
//
// WHY THE OBVIOUS PACKING IS FORBIDDEN, in the owner's own mechanism: a handle32
// is {index[31:8], generation[7:0]}, so reading this word's low sixteen bits as
// the record ID makes a RESIDENCY EVENT -- a generation bump -- silently select
// a different material and repaint geometry. "Do not read the existing word both
// as the complete set handle and as its low-16-bit material ID."
//
// THE TWO PAD ALLOCATIONS, now EXPLICIT (the ruling: "Make both allocations
// explicit in commands.zidl and regenerate ... from that source"):
//
//   payload 37..38  frame_tick    R241 D-TICK-A, PRESERVED EXACTLY. Two bytes,
//                                 little-endian, at the offset `zhao_cmd_exec`
//                                 already decodes (ZHAO_DRAW_PROCEDURAL_OFF_PAD)
//                                 and `zhao_forge_pagebank` already adds to the
//                                 page's `tick_phase_base`. It is declared
//                                 `u8[2]` rather than `u16` for ONE reason: this
//                                 file's layout law (capture_format.md 1.1
//                                 rule 2) aligns a u16 to 2 and offset 37 is
//                                 ODD, so a `u16` here is an ELABORATION ERROR
//                                 in the generator and a `u16` at 38 would MOVE
//                                 a field the ruling says to preserve.
//                                 AND DECLARING IT FIXES A REAL DEFECT: while
//                                 these were pads, the generated validator's
//                                 mandatory-zero pad list contained 37 and 38,
//                                 so a DrawProcedural carrying a NONZERO
//                                 frame_tick was REFUSED -- R241's field could
//                                 not legally be transmitted. See
//                                 ZHAO_PADS_DRAW_PROCEDURAL before and after.
//   payload 39      pad[1]        alignment for the u16 below; mandatory zero.
//   payload 40..41  material_id   NEW. u16 index within `material_set`, 4-byte
//                                 aligned (record offset 56). ZERO IS A VALID
//                                 INDEX, not a sentinel: "zero-filled legacy
//                                 material_id bytes select record 0 of the named
//                                 set."
//   payload 42..47  pad[6]        mandatory zero, still unallocated.
//
// VERSION: UNCHANGED at 3. Both allocations are same-bytes reinterpretations of
// mandatory-zero pads at unchanged offsets and sizes -- the precedent this file
// already set twice, for `forge_kind` (R108) and for the v2 `u8 mode` ->
// `video_mode` conversion. The opcode, the record size and every pre-existing
// field offset are untouched, which is this file's own additive law.
command DrawProcedural 0x0302 implemented {
  handle32[forge_program] program;
  handle32[material_set] material_set;   // the COMPLETE set handle (ruling 2)
  transform2fx transform;
  fx16 screen_error;
  forge_kind kind;     // [w3] forge family (see enum above)
  u8 frame_tick[2];    // R241 D-TICK-A, little-endian; payload 37..38
  pad[1];              // payload 39 -- alignment for material_id
  u16 material_id;     // index within material_set; 0 is a VALID record
  pad[6];              // payload 42..47
}

// Sky pass (spec/sky_and_beams.md 4 — the W4 post-patch ABI reservation).
// Reserved: layout FROZEN, execution lands in wave 8. rot_proj is
// rotation-only per view (translation rows must be zero — validated when
// the command activates). flags: b0 under_plane, b1 cloud, b2 sun, b3 cap,
// b4 sun_glow_tag; b5..b7 reserved-0. reserved0/reserved1 must be zero.
// Opcodes 0x0311..0x031F are reserved for sky extensions — never allocate
// one without a spec/sky_and_beams.md version bump. [v3: 0x0311 is now
// SetEnvironment below — 0x0312..0x031F remain reserved.]
command DrawSky 0x0310 reserved {
  handle32[sky_set] sky_set;   // sky asset set (bands/cap/under/clouds/sun)
  mat4fx rot_proj[2];          // per-view rotation-only view-projection
  fx16 cloud_scroll_u;         // cloud sheet scroll offset, u axis (turns of the sheet)
  fx16 cloud_scroll_v;         // cloud sheet scroll offset, v axis
  angle16 drum_yaw;            // sky drum yaw (U 0.0.16 turns, qformats.md 2)
  u8 viewport_mask;            // which viewports this sky applies to
  u8 flags;                    // layer enable bits (see above)
  u8 reserved0;                // must be 0
  u8 reserved1;                // must be 0
  pad[14];                     // to the 16-B record alignment (176 B record)
}

// [v3, sky_and_beams v1.2 §4a] Sky/environment extension — the FIRST
// allocation from the sky extension range (0x0311..0x031F), made under that
// file's version-bump law. Layout FROZEN since v3.
// IMPLEMENTED since owner ruling R25 (2026-09-19): "Promote SetEnvironment
// 0x0311 from reserved to IMPLEMENTED. The bank's Q16.16 / u20-gain values are
// THE LAW; section 4a's u8 formula becomes a derived view with a zref bridge.
// CMD.EXEC lowers SetEnvironment into the bank." The bridge is
// reference/include/zref/zref_light_env.hpp (bank_of); the lowering is
// zhao_cmd_exec's environment arm -> zhao_light_env -> zhao_light_stream's
// descriptor bank, loaded between vertices and committed as one generation.
// sun_yaw/sun_pitch/sun_colour/ambient reach the bank; tint and fog travel
// with the record and are NOT bank words (see the bridge header).
// VERSION: unchanged. Promotion moves no opcode, field, size or offset --
// the frame wire is byte-identical -- so by this file's own rule (the
// QFMT 1 -> 2 precedent above) it is not a command-surface change.
// The world's ONE light/environment state record —
// the donor envi.d per-level lighting struct (sun direction/colour, ambient,
// fog; S6 §1) ported to lawful widths. Per-frame GLOBAL state: no viewport
// mask (one world, one sun; Duo views share it; SetView stays the per-view
// record). Consumption laws (vertex light, global tint, fog mix order,
// defaults) live in sky_and_beams 4a; the fog formula in qformats 8.
// unit8 = qformats 2. pad[12] bytes 0-3 are the documented same-bytes site
// for a future fog_density (exponential fog — deferred, qformats 8).
command SetEnvironment 0x0311 implemented {
  angle16 sun_yaw;    // sun azimuth, turns (yaw 0 faces +Z); direction law: sky_and_beams 4a
  angle16 sun_pitch;  // sun elevation, turns (0x4000 = zenith)
  rgb565 sun_colour;  // sun colour (lanes carry the strength)
  rgb565 ambient;     // ambient colour
  rgb565 tint;        // global vertex-light tint
  u8 tint_strength;   // unit8 (qformats 2)
  fog_mode fog;       // fog law: qformats 8 (far <= near disables — deterministic no-op)
  fx16 fog_near;      // world metres
  fx16 fog_far;       // world metres
  // ABI v4+ (2026-09-26, TERRAINMAT): TERRAIN'S MATERIAL IDENTITY, allocated
  // out of this record's own mandatory-zero pad. Before it, terrain declared
  // MATMODE_NONE at GEOM.CLIP's door, published `sample_count = 0`, and asked
  // the texture island for nothing -- so no amount of correct u/v made a
  // texel (console entry I13's items (a) and (b)).
  //
  // WHY THE SAME BYTES AND NOT A NEW OPCODE. `capture_format.md` 1.3 permits
  // reinterpreting a record's declared pad when the opcode, the field set and
  // the sizes do not move; `MaterialRecord.fragment_state` is the ratified
  // precedent. The whole of the meaning rests on ZERO KEEPING ITS MEANING: a
  // zero `terrain_material_set` is MATMODE_NONE, which is exactly what every
  // committed capture's terrain declares today, so no capture changes by a
  // pixel and the `abi version` does not move (no opcode, field set or size
  // does either). The validator still zero-checks the remaining pad[6].
  //
  // SCOPE, AND ITS LIMIT IS DECLARED RATHER THAN DISCOVERED. This pair is
  // FRAME-scoped. The reference resolves terrain's tileset PER PATCH --
  // `reference/src/zrender/render_frame.cpp:373`,
  // `if (patch->tileset_id != 0) ts = res.tileset(patch->tileset_id);` -- so
  // a frame whose patches carry DIFFERENT `tileset_id`s is not expressible
  // through this pair alone. The refinement is the page header's own
  // `tileset_id` (terrain_rules 2.1 +12) overriding `terrain_material_id`
  // per patch, and it changes NO field here and NO port downstream: only what
  // drives `mat_id_i` on `zhao_terrain_clipfeed`. Recorded in console entry
  // I13 with its carriage costed. This field is a strict capability increase
  // over the zero tilesets terrain could present before it.
  handle32[material_set] terrain_material_set;  // 0 = MATMODE_NONE (today's behaviour)
  u16 terrain_material_id;                      // record within that set; the frame default
  pad[6];
}

// ---- audio (implemented in wave 3 — D7)

// [w3] EXECUTED: routes a wave-2 mixer tone (MixerTone, spec/audio_rules.md
// lane). event_id indexes the cartridge tone bank (TONE_BANK page, spec/
// cartridge.md 4 kind 5); sample_handle is the tone's sample index within
// the bank; gain/pan override the tone's declared defaults where nonzero.
// Fire-and-forget: audio failure or voice stealing NEVER changes gameplay
// truth (FORM 15). timestamp = the tick the event was emitted for.
command EmitAudioEvent 0x0400 implemented {
  u32 event_id;
  i16 pan_fx;
  u16 gain;
  u32 sample_handle;
  u32 timestamp;
}

// ---- bootstrap / debug umbrella (never game-facing; header flags bit0 required)

command DebugBootstrap 0xF001 reserved {
  u8 data[48];
}

// ABI v2 (wave 2): the two debug commands the console shell EXECUTES (plan
// W2.1/D8 — Phase-2 sinks of the CMD.SCHEDULER dispatch interface). Still
// never game-facing: a frame containing them MUST set header flags bit0.
// Wire layout (incl. reserved bytes as declared pads, so the validator
// zero-checks them per capture_format.md 1.1 rule 5):
//   dst_slot @0 u8, mode @1 video_mode, rsv @2 (2 B pad),
//   src_addr_hps @4 u32, byte_len @8 u32, expected_crc32c @12 u32,
//   rsv2+align @16 (16 B pad) — 32-B payload, 48-B record.
command DebugFrameBlit 0xF002 implemented {
  u8 dst_slot;          // framebuffer slot 0/1 the blit targets
  video_mode mode;      // mode the blit payload is laid out for
  pad[2];               // rsv
  u32 src_addr_hps;     // HPS-side source address (byte granule)
  u32 byte_len;         // blit length in bytes (must equal mode canvas bytes)
  u32 expected_crc32c;  // CRC-32C over the blit payload, checked pre-commit
  pad[16];              // rsv2 (u32) + 12-B alignment pad
}

// ABI v2 (wave 2): rumble request from the sealed frame (plan W2.1). One
// update per frame is applied (INPUT.RUMBLE latch law, spec/input_rules.md).
command DebugRumble 0xF004 implemented {
  u8 pad_index;   // 0-3
  u8 enable;      // 0 = stop, nonzero = run
  u8 strength;    // PWM duty numerator (duty = strength/256)
  pad[13];        // rsv byte + 12-B alignment pad — 16-B payload, 32-B record
}

// ---- resources (owner ruling R17, 2026-09-19) --------------------------------
//
// PublishResource: THE ONE COMMAND THAT MOVES A STAGED RESOURCE INTO VRAM.
// Ruling R17 (reports/OWNER-RULINGS-20260919-EVENING.md): "a new ratified
// command ... lowered by CMD.EXEC onto MEM.UPLOAD's request port". Every field
// is one of MEM.UPLOAD's request fields (design/contracts/MEM.UPLOAD.md
// `UploadRequest`), and nothing here is interpreted by the command path:
//
//   resource        the handle32 the game names the resource by. Its 24-bit
//                   INDEX is spec/memory_rules.md 5f.1's directory key; its
//                   8-bit generation is the handle's, NOT the residency
//                   generation (that is `new_generation`, 16 bits -- D-3's
//                   cache tag keys on all sixteen).
//   hps_addr_lo/hi  the staged bytes in the HPS arena. SIXTY-FOUR bits on
//                   purpose: MEM.UPLOAD REFUSES a source above 4 GiB
//                   (kUploadSourceUnreachable) rather than narrowing it, and a
//                   32-bit field would do the narrowing on the wire.
//   vram_dst        destination in local SDRAM (the allocator's FRESH slot).
//   length          bytes, a multiple of 64 (a refusal, never a pad).
//   crc32c          over the staged bytes, zhao_crc32c_fold's law.
//   new_generation  the residency generation published on completion.
//   epoch           the resource epoch this upload belongs to. NOT in R17's
//                   field list and added deliberately: the contract's
//                   UploadRequest carries it and its law 2 is "a request naming
//                   an epoch that has closed is REFUSED" -- a command without
//                   it could only borrow somebody else's epoch.
//   dst_slot        the arena slot (MEM.UPLOAD's `req_dst_slot_i`).
//   kind            the .zpak resource kind (spec/cartridge.md 4a), which
//                   travels as MEM.UPLOAD's `req_tag_i` and is published as
//                   the directory row's kind.
//
// VERSION DECISION: `abi version` STAYS 3, the precedent of TerrainEpoch
// 0x0220 / SubmitTerrainSet 0x0230, which were allocated under v3 by ruling T5
// without a bump. A v3 decoder built before this line reports
// ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE on 0x0030 -- a clean refusal -- and every committed
// capture stays valid, because no opcode, field set or size it uses moved.
command PublishResource 0x0030 implemented {
  handle32[resource] resource;
  u32 hps_addr_lo;
  u32 hps_addr_hi;
  u32 vram_dst;
  u32 length;
  u32 crc32c;
  u16 new_generation;
  u16 epoch;
  u8  dst_slot;
  u8  kind;
  pad[2];
}

// ---- post look and grading (owner rulings R35/R36, 2026-09-19) ---------------
//
// SetPost: POST.COMPOSITE's per-frame LOOK. Ruling R36: "Ratify a `SetPost`
// command carrying bloom gain/bias, flash, ink, grade-valid and the echo arm
// (R35), plus a grading-table load, lowered by CMD.EXEC." Every field is one of
// POST.COMPOSITE's look inputs (fpga/rtl/compositor/zhao_post_composite.sv),
// carried at the width the block consumes or wider, and nothing is interpreted
// on the way:
//
//   bloom_gain     unit8 (qformats 2): the bloom add's gain, stage 4.
//   flags          bit0 GRADE_VALID -- the palette curves + matrix (stage 5-7)
//                  apply; 0 passes colour through ungraded.
//                  bit1 ECHO_ARM -- POST.ECHO captures THIS frame (ruling R35:
//                  "Capture is ARMED, not always-on"). 0 = no capture, and no
//                  capture traffic.
//                  bits 7:2 UNASSIGNED and REFUSED if set: CMD.EXEC drops the
//                  record and counts it, it never masks a bit it does not know.
//   flash_amount   unit8: the flash/tint lerp amount, stage 8. 0 = no flash.
//   bias_r/g/b     the grade's post-matrix bias, added after the round and
//                  before the saturate (zref::post::grade_finalize). The block
//                  takes signed NINE bits, so the legal range is [-256, 255];
//                  a record outside it is REFUSED whole, never clamped.
//   flash          rgb565, the flash/tint colour.
//   ink            rgb565, the exterior-ink colour, stage 9.
//
// THE LOOK CHANGES ONLY BETWEEN POST PASSES. CMD.EXEC applies a committed
// SetPost (and streams a committed grading table) only while the post lease is
// idle, and it does so before the packet's draws leave -- so frame N's look is
// in place before frame N's raster starts, and never under a pass in flight.
//
// SetGradeTable: up to EIGHT entries of one palette curve's PRODUCT-VECTOR
// table -- the owner plan 11.2 exact preparation zref::post::grade_product_vector
// generates: an entry is that curve value times its own column of the signed
// Q2.14 matrix, three signed 24-bit products {outR, outG, outB}, little-endian,
// nine bytes each, entry k at vectors[9k .. 9k+8]. Curves are R (32 entries),
// G (64) and B (32); `first + count` must fit the curve, `count` is 1..8, and
// curve 3 does not exist -- any of those is REFUSED whole. A full table is 16
// records. Bytes of `vectors` past `count` entries are carried and ignored.
//
// VERSION DECISION: `abi version` STAYS 3, the PublishResource 0x0030 precedent
// (and TerrainEpoch/SubmitTerrainSet before it): an additive opcode moves no
// existing opcode, field set or size, so every committed capture stays valid and
// a decoder built before this line reports ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE -- a clean
// refusal. Declared LAST so no existing golden's sample values shift.
command SetPost 0x0040 implemented {
  u8 bloom_gain;      // unit8
  u8 flags;           // bit0 grade_valid, bit1 echo_arm; bits 7:2 refused
  u8 flash_amount;    // unit8
  pad[1];
  i16 bias_r;         // [-256, 255]
  i16 bias_g;
  i16 bias_b;
  rgb565 flash;
  rgb565 ink;
  pad[2];
}

command SetGradeTable 0x0041 implemented {
  u8 curve;           // 0 = R[32], 1 = G[64], 2 = B[32]
  u8 first;           // first entry this record loads
  u8 count;           // 1..8
  pad[1];
  u8 vectors[72];     // count x {outR s24, outG s24, outB s24}, little-endian
  pad[4];
}

// SetPopulation: THE POPULATION DESCRIPTOR'S FRAME VALUES, owner ruling R41
// (reports/OWNER-RULINGS-20260919-EVENING.md): "Ratify `SetPopulation`
// (origin, plane, active_count), lowered by CMD.EXEC. active_count also seeds
// PART.STATE's first generation, replacing I1's provisional HPS seed."
//
// It closes core entry I7. Everything in it was already a LIVE INPUT of the
// particle engine with no ratified carrier -- the composer drove them from
// board pins, which is the shape the completion register calls a boundary:
//
//   population      the handle32 the game names the pool by, exactly as
//                   DrawPopulation 0x0301 names it. Carried so a capture can
//                   be read without guessing which pool a descriptor is for;
//                   v1 hardware holds ONE population's descriptor and the
//                   bank records the handle it last took.
//   origin_x/y/z    the population origin. spec/qformats.md 10: "origin x/y/z
//                   as fx16 ON A 1/256-M GRID" and "World position = origin +
//                   local". DECLARED i32 AND NOT fx16 DELIBERATELY: this
//                   file's fx16 is Q16.16 in four bytes, and the origin's
//                   grid is 1/256 m -- eight fractional bits. The container is
//                   the same four bytes either way, so nothing on the wire
//                   depends on the choice; the NAME is what a reader converts
//                   by, and Q16.16 would be wrong by 256. The law is
//                   `zhao_part_terrain_tap`'s: world = origin + (local <<< 8).
//   active_count    records live in the first generation. It is the seed:
//                   children come from parents, so a store that starts empty
//                   stays empty (see `zhao_part_hps`). THE FIRST GENERATION IS
//                   STAGED IN BUFFER 0, by this ratification -- the HPS writes
//                   it there before the frame that carries the seed. The two
//                   buffer BASES stay the HPS's allocation (spec/memory_rules.md
//                   5, "particle pools per the charter allocator") and are not
//                   a command field: an allocator address in a game-facing
//                   record is a different decision and nobody has made it.
//   plane_c         the analytic collision plane's constant, Q10 (PART.COLLIDE
//                   `NRM_Q`); the surface is n.p = c.
//   plane_nx/ny/nz  the plane's unit normal, signed Q1.10. i16 on the wire;
//                   PART.COLLIDE carries a SIGNED 12-bit component, so a value
//                   outside [-2048, 2047] cannot be represented. It is REFUSED AND
//                   COUNTED by `zhao_part_pop`, never truncated -- a silently
//                   truncated normal is a plane that tilts.
//   flags           b0 seed_first_generation (take active_count as the store's
//                   seed), b1 plane_enable (b1 clear = no analytic plane, and
//                   the terrain is still sampled). b2..b15 reserved 0.
//
// VERSION DECISION: `abi version` STAYS 3, on the PublishResource 0x0030
// precedent recorded below. 0x0303 is the next free opcode in the
// forms/populations range (0x0300 DrawForm, 0x0301 DrawPopulation, 0x0302
// DrawProcedural); no opcode, field or size of an existing command moves, so
// every committed capture stays valid and a v3 decoder built before this line
// reports ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE on 0x0303, which is a clean refusal.
command SetPopulation 0x0303 implemented {
  handle32[population] population;
  i32 origin_x;        // 1/256-m grid (see above) -- NOT Q16.16
  i32 origin_y;
  i32 origin_z;
  u32 active_count;    // records live in the first generation, staged in buffer 0
  i32 plane_c;         // Q10; the surface is n.p = c
  i16 plane_nx;        // Q1.10 unit normal, -2048..2047 (signed 12 bits)
  i16 plane_ny;
  i16 plane_nz;
  u16 flags;           // b0 seed_first_generation, b1 plane_enable; b2-15 rsv 0
}

// ---- DEBUG.TRACE arming (owner ruling R52, 2026-09-19) ----------------------
//
// DebugTraceArm: THE ONE COMMAND THAT ARMS THE TRACE RING. Ruling R52
// (reports/OWNER-RULINGS-20260919-EVENING.md): "Ratify `DebugTraceArm` in the
// reserved 0xF0xx debug range, lowered by CMD.EXEC. ABI addition: zidl, zref
// and captures move together."
//
// WHY A COMMAND AND NOT A CSR. `zhao_host_regwin` (ruling R51) gives the HPS a
// register aperture, and arming through it would have been one line. Ruling
// R18's principle decides against it: ONE AUTHORITY PER LEVEL. A ring armed
// from the command stream and also from a register has two writers with no
// ordering between them, so a capture could not be attributed to the packet
// that asked for it. `armed` is READABLE at the aperture (tenant 1, word
// 0x200) and writable only here.
//
// WHEN IT TAKES EFFECT, AND THE SENTENCE NEEDS ITS QUALIFIERS. CMD.EXEC
// applies the mask at this record's LAST BYTE, during the walk. CMD.DECODER
// offers a record to the ring at the record's byte 15 (the end of its header).
//
// The first version of this comment concluded from that, flatly, that "the
// DebugTraceArm record itself is NOT traced; every record after it in the same
// packet IS", and called it a guarantee. BOTH HALVES ARE OVER-BROAD -- found by
// review 2026-09-20, corrected here by ruling R108's bundle, and the corrected
// text is lifted from `zhao_cmd_exec.sv`'s R52 port comment (:501-527) rather
// than re-derived, so the ABI and the block that implements it cannot drift.
// An over-broad guarantee is worse than a hedged one, because somebody writes
// a test against it:
//
//   * THE ARM IS NOT TRACED only when stage 0 was not ALREADY armed. A SECOND
//     DebugTraceArm, in a packet whose ring is already watching the decoder,
//     IS offered to the ring at its own byte 15 and IS stored -- correctly,
//     because by then it is just another record.
//   * EVERY LATER RECORD IS TRACED only if the arm was ACCEPTED (a reserved
//     bit refuses it whole), if the mask actually sets bit 0, and while the
//     ring has room -- a full ring DROPS and counts, it does not stall the
//     walk.
//
// What IS unconditional is the TIMING, and that is the part worth having:
// the mask is applied at the arming record's LAST byte and the decoder offers
// a record at its byte 15, so no record can be offered between the two. The
// next header cannot complete for at least sixteen more byte-cycles. Nothing
// here is a race; the qualifiers are all about whether a store happens at all,
// never about when.
//
// So the store count is `N - P`, not `N - 2`: N records in the packet, P the
// 1-based position of the first ACCEPTED bit-0 arm.
//
// It is applied WITHOUT waiting for the packet's verdict, unlike every other
// command CMD.EXEC executes. The trace surface is already speculative by the
// decoder's own contract ("a record that may still be rejected"), and a ring
// that could not observe a packet that FAILS would be blind to the one packet
// anybody is debugging.
//
// STAGE NUMBERS are charter 20.6's, and DEBUG.TRACE's `arm_mask_i` is a MASK
// rather than a selector so two stages can be traced in one run:
//   bit 0 command decoder   bit 1 vertex output    bit 2 clipped triangle
//   bit 3 tile insertion    bit 4 texture address  bit 5 depth test
//   bit 6 final pixel
// Only bit 0 has a producer in the v1 console; `zhao_console_core` header
// entry I18 argues why the other six do not, and arming them stores nothing
// rather than storing something invented.
//
// 0xF003 was the one unallocated opcode between DebugFrameBlit 0xF002 and
// DebugRumble 0xF004. `abi version` STAYS 3, the PublishResource/TerrainEpoch
// precedent: a v3 decoder built before this line reports
// ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE on 0xF003, which is a clean refusal.
//
// Wire layout: stage_mask @0 u8, flags @1 u8, pad @2 (14 B) -- 16-B payload,
// 32-B record. A frame containing it MUST set header flags bit0
// (ZH_ABI_DEBUG_FLAG_REQUIRED), like every other 0xF0nn opcode.
command DebugTraceArm 0xF003 implemented {
  u8 stage_mask;  // bit n arms stage n; bit 7 must be 0
  u8 flags;       // bit0 = clear the ring and the drop count; bits 1-7 reserved 0
  pad[14];        // rsv -- 16-B payload, 32-B record
}

// ---- posed creature draw (owner ruling R229, 2026-09-21) --------------------
//
// DrawPosedForm: THE ONE COMMAND THAT NAMES WHICH ANIMATION FRAME A DRAW IS IN.
// Ruling R229 (reports/OWNER-RULINGS-20260919-EVENING.md), decision
// D-POSEPAGE-A, in its own words: "take `DrawPosedForm` at 0x0305, carrying
// {clip_id, frame_no, sub}, with `DrawForm` keeping its meaning as bind pose".
//
// It spends a deferral that was recorded eighteen days earlier and never cited:
// `reports/ZHAOZHOU_ANIMATION_HPS_RESIDENCY_ARCHITECTURE.md` (owner-ratified
// 2026-09-03) 4.2 says in terms that "the exact command-record representation
// is deferred". THIS IS THAT REPRESENTATION, and nothing more than it.
//
// WHY A PER-DRAW RECORD AND NOT A `SetPose` STATE COMMAND. The alternative was
// raised fairly on SetPopulation 0x0303's precedent and R229 refused it: POSE
// VARIES PER CREATURE. Ruling R13's clause is the governing analogy -- "the job
// port is not widened to carry a subpatch-uniform value that is not true" --
// and a pose placed in STATE is that same error one level up, a per-draw
// quantity in a carrier whose shape claims it is uniform. A `SetPose` before
// every `DrawForm` is the same byte count with an ordering hazard added.
//
// THE FIRST SIXTEEN PAYLOAD BYTES ARE `DrawForm`'s, BYTE FOR BYTE, and that is
// the whole of R229's "clean split that breaks no existing content":
//
//     offset     0            4              8           12       13
//     DrawForm   form         material_set   transform   vp_mask  weight
//     offset     14           16             18          20       21..31
//     DrawForm   flags        --             --          --       --
//     this       flags        clip_id        frame_no    sub      pad
//
// `DrawForm` 0x0300 is UNTOUCHED and keeps its meaning: a draw with no clip
// named is the BIND POSE. Every committed capture stays valid; a v3 decoder
// built before this line reports ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE on 0x0305, a clean
// refusal. Sharing the prefix is not a convenience -- it is what lets CMD.EXEC
// capture both opcodes with ONE set of field offsets, so the executor cannot
// develop a second opinion about where a form handle lives.
//
// THE FIELDS, and why each is the width it is. Every one is a lane of the pose
// cache's KEY (`fpga/rtl/geometry/zhao_geom_pose_cache.sv`, tag layout
// [15:0] type [31:16] clip [47:32] frame [55:48] sub), carried at the width
// that block consumes:
//
//   clip_id    the clip's SLOT ID, which is `zref::clip_page`'s directory key
//              (`kOffSlotId`, u16) and `spec/creature_rules.md` 5's own
//              `slot_id u16`. NOT a row index: the bank answers a lookup by
//              slot, and a page may order its rows freely.
//              `creature_rules` 2.1 freezes "64 authored slots"
//              (`zref::clip_page::kMaxClips`), so a slot at or above 64 names
//              a row no legal page can contain -- REFUSED AND COUNTED by
//              `zhao_cmd_exec` (`pose_clip_refused_o`), never truncated. That
//              is REPRESENTABILITY, not resolvability: whether a page actually
//              HOLDS clip 7 is the clip bank's judgement and this command
//              surface has no opinion on it. Same law as SetPopulation's
//              `plane_nx` -- a value the consumer cannot represent is refused
//              whole rather than silently narrowed.
//   frame_no   the key index within the clip, u16, matching the directory's
//              own `frame_count u16` (`zref::clip_page::kOffFrameCount`) and
//              the cache's `acq_frame_i [15:0]`. A frame past the clip's end
//              is `acq_resolvable_i` low -- the cache's rule 1, BAD_ID, bind
//              pose -- and is likewise not this surface's judgement to make.
//   sub        THE HALF-KEY PHASE, and IT IS NOT PADDING. The cache's own
//              header records what omitting it cost: with baked 60 Hz
//              presentation data "a key and its midpoint had the SAME
//              {type, clip, frame} and aliased -- the cache returned the wrong
//              palette and nothing reported an error". The reference
//              `zref::creature::PoseBank::acquire(type, slot, frame, sub)` has
//              always carried it. u8, exactly `acq_sub_i [7:0]`.
//
// WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, so nobody reads a hole as an oversight:
//
//   type_id    NOT a field. The pose cache's `acq_type_i` is the CREATURE TYPE,
//              and the draw already names it: `form` is the form resource
//              handle and its 24-bit index is `spec/memory_rules.md` 5f.1's
//              directory key. Carrying a second identity for one creature
//              beside the first is the two-sources-of-truth shape this repo
//              keeps finding; whoever resolves `form` to a type owes that
//              mapping a directed check, and owes it in ONE place.
//   generation NOT a field, and this is the ruling's stated boundary. R229:
//   / epoch    "4.2's request-side representation -- a validated resident
//              handle with generation and epoch, not a naked slot and frame --
//              is a DIFFERENT LAYER and remains undetermined." The residency
//              generation is published by `PublishResource` 0x0030's
//              `new_generation` and is the resident-handle layer's to carry.
//              A game-facing record cannot state a generation it does not own.
//
// VERSION DECISION: `abi version` STAYS 3, on the PublishResource 0x0030 /
// TerrainEpoch 0x0220 / SetPost 0x0040 / SetPopulation 0x0303 / DebugTraceArm
// 0xF003 precedent -- five times over. No opcode, field set or size of an
// existing command moves, so every committed capture stays valid.
//
// APPENDED AT THE END OF THE FILE, under owner ruling R171's standing
// instruction for exactly this range: "Inserting beside `DrawForm` rewrites
// nine goldens, and a golden rewrite is a change nobody can review." The reason
// is mechanical, not stylistic -- `tools/abi-gen/src/sample.ts` stamps a
// sample's `source_id` from the command's INDEX in this file, so an insert
// renumbers every command after it and churns their goldens for no change in
// meaning. Position in the file carries no semantics; the opcode does.
//
// 0x0305 AND NOT 0x0304. 0x0304 IS SPOKEN FOR -- plan W04 allocates it to
// `DrawWarpedForm` (reports/OWNER-RATIFICATION-20260920-WARP.md, ruling R171)
// and it is not yet in this file, so reading the file alone makes it look free.
// It is not. The next free draw opcode is 0x0305. 0x0306..0x030F remain free;
// 0x0310 is DrawSky and 0x0311..0x031F stay sky-reserved.
command DrawPosedForm 0x0305 implemented {
  handle32[form] form;
  handle32[material_set] material_set;
  handle32[transform] transform;
  u8 viewport_mask;
  u8 semantic_weight;
  u16 flags;           // DrawForm 0x0300's flags, same bits, same meanings
  u16 clip_id;         // clip SLOT id (creature_rules 5); >= 64 is REFUSED
  u16 frame_no;        // key index within the clip
  u8  sub;             // half-key phase -- part of the cache KEY, not padding
  pad[11];             // rsv -- 32-B payload, 48-B record
}

// ---- warped creature/form draw (owner directive W04, 2026-09-20) ------------
//
// DrawWarpedForm: THE ONE COMMAND THAT CAN TURN WARP ON. Until this line
// existed, `zhao_geom_warp.sv` and `zhao_field_warp_adapter.sv` were both BUILT
// and both STRUCTURALLY UNREACHABLE -- there was no draw that could set
// `d_warp_en_i`, so a composed Warp would have sat permanently in its W09
// bypass. That is not a missing feature at the edge of the design; it is the
// reason the block could not be composed at all, and it is recorded as such in
// `design/contracts/GEOM.WARP.md`'s prerequisite table.
//
// AUTHORITY. Decision W04 of the owner directive
// `reports/Zhaozhou_GEOM_WARP_Architecture_2026-09-20.txt` (rev 1.1, owner
// commit `4c256137`, Fabian, 2026-09-20), ratified in
// `reports/OWNER-RATIFICATION-20260920-WARP.md`: "Add `DrawWarpedForm` at
// opcode 0x0304, 96-byte record / 80-byte payload. `DrawForm 0x0300` and raw
// vertex format 0 stay byte-for-byte unchanged. 0x0312-0x031F remain
// sky-reserved." The layout below is directive 6.1's, field for field.
//
// 0x0304 WAS RESERVED IN PROSE BEFORE IT WAS RESERVED IN GRAMMAR, and the
// `DrawPosedForm 0x0305` note above says so in as many words: "0x0304 IS
// SPOKEN FOR -- plan W04 allocates it to `DrawWarpedForm` ... and it is not yet
// in this file, so reading the file alone makes it look free." This line is
// what makes the file agree with the plan. Re-verified free at this commit:
// 0x0304 appears in no other `command` declaration here.
//
// THE FIRST SIXTEEN PAYLOAD BYTES ARE `DrawForm`'s, BYTE FOR BYTE -- the same
// discipline `DrawPosedForm` adopted, and for the same mechanical reason: it
// lets CMD.EXEC capture all three draw opcodes with ONE set of field offsets,
// so the executor cannot develop a second opinion about where a form handle
// lives.
//
//     offset     0            4              8           12       13
//     DrawForm   form         material_set   transform   vp_mask  weight
//     offset     14           16             20          24       40
//     DrawForm   flags        --             --          --       --
//     this       flags        warp_program   time        params   attributes
//     offset     56             60         61          62    64      76
//     this       warp_attrs     attr_mode  warp_flags  rsv   bound   rsv
//
// `DrawForm` 0x0300 is UNTOUCHED and keeps its meaning: a draw that names no
// Warp program is an ORDINARY draw and W09 requires it to perform zero Warp
// lookups and zero Warp evaluations. Every committed capture stays valid; a
// decoder built before this line reports ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE on 0x0304, a
// clean refusal. Raw vertex format 0 is not touched here or anywhere -- W04
// says byte-for-byte and directive section A puts "reinterpreting reserved
// bytes" of format 0 on the prohibited list.
//
// NO HIDDEN STATE, and this is decision W05 rather than a taste. Directive 6.2
// refuses `SetWarp` + ordinary `DrawForm` BY NAME: CMD.EXEC groups some state
// updates before draws, so a mutable last-writer `current_warp` register could
// RETROACTIVELY CHANGE OLDER DRAWS. It equally refuses making every `DrawForm`
// read a mutable per-instance Warp table, which would change the meaning of old
// commands. This record carries its own snapshot -- program, time, params,
// attribute mode, attribute resource and displacement bound all belong to THIS
// draw -- and avoids that entire class. It is the same argument `DrawPosedForm`
// makes against `SetPose`, one level along.
//
// THE FIELDS, and why each is here.
//
//   warp_program   the W-profile field program. A `program` handle, the SAME
//                  kind `TerrainField 0x0200` uses for the Earth profile, and
//                  for the same reason: it names a cartridge PROGRAM page and
//                  it is resolved by the ONE shared program-binding authority
//                  (W07) -- handle -> canonical program -> prepared plan /
//                  resident slot. W07 is explicit that "a handle is not a
//                  content hash; a content hash is not a physical resident
//                  slot", so this field is a HANDLE and nothing else. Zero
//                  means NO WARP: an ordinary draw that happens to use this
//                  opcode, which is legal and is the bypass W09 protects.
//   time           u32 TICK DATA, bit-cast and not converted, canonical input
//                  lane 10. THIS DRAW'S tick and never a clock read -- a Warp
//                  evaluated from a free-running counter would give two
//                  different answers to the two cameras, and GEOM.WARP is
//                  VIEW-INDEPENDENT by contract section 1.
//   params[4]      p0..p3, canonical input lanes 11..14. FOUR, not three:
//                  directive conflict C01 records that `spec/form/field-ir.md`
//                  7.1 listed fifteen warp input fields and then wrote "(14)"
//                  after them, and decision W01 rules that THE FIELDS ARE RIGHT
//                  AND THE COUNT WAS WRONG. Building to fourteen drops p3, and
//                  a dropped lane does not read as missing -- it reads as
//                  whatever the Field front cleared that register to.
//   attributes[4]  a0..a3 INLINE4, canonical input lanes 6..9. Constant across
//                  the draw. Must be zero under STREAM4.
//   warp_attributes  the versioned WARP_ATTRIBUTES resource for STREAM4, a
//                  `resource` handle on `PublishResource 0x0030`'s generation
//                  law. Must be zero under INLINE4. W06 forbids the three
//                  cheaper alternatives BY NAME: do not steal format-0 reserved
//                  bytes, do not commandeer vertex formats 1/2, and do not
//                  synthesize attributes from guessed UV units.
//   attribute_mode   the enum above. Generated legality, ZH_ABI_BAD_VALUE.
//   warp_flags     reserved zero in this revision. A future flag lands here and
//                  not in `flags`, which is `DrawForm`'s word and keeps
//                  `DrawForm`'s bit meanings including R28's cull mode.
//   displacement_bound[3]
//                  THE W11 DECLARATION, and it is load-bearing in two separate
//                  places rather than one. Visibility is conservative BEFORE
//                  fetch and deform, so MESHFETCH/CULL expand the draw's
//                  world-space bounds by this triple before culling and account
//                  for it in LOD error; and the RETURNED displacement is
//                  runtime-checked against it, |d[k]| > bound[k] POISONING
//                  the meshlet. Each component is a NONNEGATIVE signed fx: a
//                  negative one is a DRAW_INVALID refused before any meshlet is
//                  emitted (contract section 9), never absolute-valued into
//                  something usable. And directive 5.6: "do not clamp the
//                  displacement to the bound and pretend the program computed
//                  that clamp" -- `zhao_geom_warp` preserves the offending
//                  value on its poison port precisely so the evidence survives
//                  the refusal.
//
// WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT.
//
//   clip_id /      NOT fields. This is `DrawForm`'s extension, not
//   frame_no / sub `DrawPosedForm`'s. A warped POSED draw is a third opcode if
//                  the owner ever asks for one; synthesising it by widening
//                  this record would make two commands' payloads disagree about
//                  what lives at offset 16, which is the one property the
//                  shared 16-byte prefix exists to guarantee.
//   amplitude /    NOT fields, and W03 forbids them BY NAME along with a
//   blend weight   Jacobian, finite differences and any extra normalization.
//                  The normal-deformation law is authored by the WARP PROGRAM
//                  (W17), not by the command surface and not by the shell.
//   generation /   NOT fields, on `DrawPosedForm`'s stated boundary: the
//   epoch          residency generation is published by `PublishResource
//                  0x0030` and belongs to the resident-handle layer. A
//                  game-facing record cannot state a generation it does not own.
//
// VERSION DECISION: `abi version` STAYS 3. Directive 6.4 asks for exactly this
// and asks that the decision be RECORDED rather than inherited from
// contradictory historical comments. The precedent is now six deep --
// PublishResource 0x0030 / TerrainEpoch 0x0220 / SetPost 0x0040 /
// SetPopulation 0x0303 / DebugTraceArm 0xF003 / DrawPosedForm 0x0305. No
// opcode, field set, size or offset of an existing command moves, so every
// committed capture stays valid and old decoders reject the unknown opcode.
//
// APPENDED AT THE END OF THE FILE, under owner ruling R171: `sample.ts` stamps
// a sample's `source_id` from the command's INDEX in this file, so an insert
// beside `DrawForm` renumbers every command after it and churns nine goldens
// for no change in meaning. Position carries no semantics; the opcode does.
//
// 0x0306..0x030F remain free; 0x0310 is DrawSky and 0x0311 is SetEnvironment,
// with 0x0312..0x031F still sky-reserved (W04 restates that reservation).
command DrawWarpedForm 0x0304 implemented {
  handle32[form] form;
  handle32[material_set] material_set;
  handle32[transform] transform;
  u8 viewport_mask;
  u8 semantic_weight;
  u16 flags;                        // DrawForm 0x0300's flags, same bits
  handle32[program] warp_program;   // W-profile program; 0 = no warp (W09 bypass)
  u32 time;                         // THIS draw's tick, lane 10; never a clock read
  fx16 params[4];                   // p0..p3, lanes 11..14 (FOUR -- W01)
  fx16 attributes[4];               // a0..a3 INLINE4, lanes 6..9
  handle32[resource] warp_attributes;  // STREAM4 source; 0 under INLINE4
  warp_attribute_mode attribute_mode;  // generated legality: ZH_ABI_BAD_VALUE
  u8 warp_flags;                    // reserved 0 in this revision
  pad[2];                           // rsv
  fx16 displacement_bound[3];       // W11, each >= 0, world-space componentwise
  pad[4];                           // rsv -- 80-B payload, 96-B record (W04)
}

// ---- TWOD: the two descriptor producers (owner ruling 2026-09-22, item 3) ----
//
// RATIFIED: `reports/Zhaozhou_proposed_completion_rulings_2026-09-22.txt`
// section 3, adopted by Fabian on 2026-09-22 and recorded in
// `reports/OWNER-RATIFICATION-20260922-COMPLETION.md`.
//
//   "Authorize command-side control for BOTH existing TWOD descriptor paths,
//    not merely an opcode named SetPlane."
//
// THE TWO PATHS HAVE DIFFERENT CONSUMERS and that is why there are two records
// rather than one. `SetPlane` programs the restricted BACKDROP/ATMOSPHERE
// engine (`fpga/rtl/compositor/zhao_twod_plane.sv`); `DrawSprite` supplies the
// HUD sprite descriptor the walker and the band consume
// (`zhao_twod_sprite.sv`, `zhao_twod_band.sv`). The ruling: "Adding only a
// plane command does not establish a producer for HUD sprite descriptors."
//
// OPCODES 0x0306 AND 0x0307 WERE VERIFIED FREE against this file before they
// were taken: 0x0300..0x0305 are DrawForm / DrawPopulation / DrawProcedural /
// SetPopulation / DrawWarpedForm / DrawPosedForm, and 0x0310..0x031F are
// sky-reserved. The ruling's own words: "Do not reuse 0x0303-0x0305 or the
// sky-reserved range."
//
// VERSION DECISION: `abi version` STAYS 3 -- the precedent is now seven deep
// (PublishResource 0x0030, TerrainEpoch 0x0220, SubmitTerrainSet 0x0230,
// SetPost 0x0040, SetPopulation 0x0303, DebugTraceArm 0xF003,
// DrawPosedForm 0x0305, DrawWarpedForm 0x0304). No opcode, field set, size or
// offset of an existing command moves, so every committed capture stays valid
// and a decoder built before this line reports ZH_ABI_UNKNOWN_OPCODE -- a clean
// refusal.
//
// APPENDED AT THE END OF THE FILE, under owner ruling R171 and the ruling's own
// "Append declarations so unrelated generated samples are not renumbered".
//
// WHY THESE FIELDS ARE PLAIN u8 AND NOT ENUMS, which is a deliberate refusal
// rather than laziness. An `enum` here would make an out-of-range `role` a
// ZH_ABI_BAD_VALUE and FAIL THE WHOLE FRAME at validation. `TWOD.PLANE.md`'s
// table says a role of 2 or 3 REFUSES THE DESCRIPTOR AND COUNTS, and the frame
// completes; `TWOD.SPRITE.md` says the same of an unknown format and of a zero
// extent. The ruling requires "Retain existing malformed-descriptor refusal
// rules", so the malformed value must reach the consumer that owns the
// refusal. The generated validator therefore checks STRUCTURE -- length,
// alignment, mandatory-zero pads -- and the CONSUMER judges the VALUE.
//
// 0x0308..0x030F remain free after these two.

// SetPlane: ONE restricted plane slot, programmed whole.
//
// Field for field it is `zhao_twod_plane`'s `d_*` group plus the three the
// sampler needs to find the texels (base, lstride, lheight -- its `ld_bind_*`)
// and the atmosphere sheet's line_scroll. NOTHING IS INVENTED: there is no
// depth field, no second texture unit, no bilinear selector and no role beyond
// the two `TWOD.PLANE.md` declares -- the ruling's "It does not invent a
// depth-tested HUD plane or a second unrestricted texture unit."
//
//   slot        0 or 1. The two-slot limit is REAL (owner 2026-08-31 3.1).
//   role        0 BACKDROP, 1 ATMOSPHERE. 2 and 3 are reserved and the
//               CONSUMER refuses them (refused_role_o).
//   blend       0 REPLACE, 1 ALPHA, 2 ADD. A BACKDROP asking for anything but
//               REPLACE is refused by the consumer (refused_blend_o).
//   opacity     unit8 (qformats 2): value = raw/256.
//   format      0 CLUT8, 1 RGB565. There is no third.
//   wrap        b0 wrap_u, b1 wrap_v; 0 = repeat, 1 = clamp. b7:2 MUST be 0.
//   view_mask   b1:0, one bit per Duo view. b7:2 MUST be 0.
//   palette_id  CLUT8 palette slot.
//   width       texels across the plane's page region.
//   height      texels down it.
//   flags       b0 ENABLE. 0 DISABLES the slot for this frame and is a LAWFUL
//               record, not a refusal -- the ruling's "explicit plane disable
//               behavior". b15:1 MUST be 0.
//   base        first 16-bit word of the region inside the TWOD page store.
//   lstride     log2 of the words per row of that region.
//   lheight     log2 of the rows.
//   a,b,c,d     du/dx, du/dy, dv/dx, dv/dy -- the affine, fx16.
//   u0,v0       u and v at screen (0,0), fx16.
//   line_scroll the per-line u offset applied to the ATMOSPHERE sheet, fx16.
//
// A SLOT THE FRAME NEVER NAMES IS DISABLED FOR THAT FRAME. `TWOD.PLANE.md`:
// "no descriptor state survives a reset, because descriptors are RE-SENT PER
// FRAME". That is what makes the plane frame-scoped in the same sense the
// sprite list is, and it is what gives the ruling's empty frame a defined
// answer instead of the previous frame's sky.
command SetPlane 0x0306 implemented {
  u8   slot;
  u8   role;
  u8   blend;
  u8   opacity;       // unit8
  u8   format;
  u8   wrap;          // b0 wrap_u, b1 wrap_v; b7:2 = 0
  u8   view_mask;     // b1:0; b7:2 = 0
  u8   palette_id;
  u16  width;
  u16  height;
  u16  flags;         // b0 ENABLE; b15:1 = 0
  u16  base;          // page-store word address of the plane's texels
  u8   lstride;       // log2 words per row
  u8   lheight;       // log2 rows
  pad[2];
  fx16 a;             // du/dx
  fx16 b;             // du/dy
  fx16 c;             // dv/dx
  fx16 d;             // dv/dy
  fx16 u0;
  fx16 v0;
  fx16 line_scroll;   // ATMOSPHERE sheet's per-line u offset
}

// DrawSprite: ONE HUD sprite descriptor.
//
// Field for field it is `zhao_twod_sprite`'s `d_*` group -- which is also
// `zhao_twod_band`'s, because the band hands the walker its own record
// band-clipped -- plus the three the sampler needs to find the texels.
//
// TEXT IS GLYPH SPRITES. The ruling: "no new font engine, text-layout engine
// or private general sampler. Text remains glyph sprites authored by
// software." A line of text is N of these records, and the console contains
// nothing that knows what a glyph is.
//
//   x, y        top-left in screen pixels, SIGNED so a sprite may hang off the
//               left or top edge and be clipped rather than refused.
//   w, h        extent in pixels. Zero in either is REFUSED by the consumer
//               (zhao_twod_sprite.refused_o), never by the frame validator.
//   base        first 16-bit word of this sprite's region in the page store.
//   lstride     log2 words per row of that region.
//   lheight     log2 rows.
//   format      0 CLUT8, 1 RGB565; anything else the SAMPLER refuses
//               (fmt_refused_o).
//   palette_id  CLUT8 palette slot.
//   blend       carried to the band and COUNTED THERE AS UNAPPLIED
//               (twod_band_blend_dropped_o). POST.COMPOSITE's HUD stage is a
//               REPLACE, so a HUD blend against the world cannot be computed in
//               a store; the gap is a NUMBER rather than a sentence, and it was
//               declared before this command existed.
//   view_mask   b1:0. Both player HUD regions are addressed by this and by `y`
//               -- the Duo seam is a ROW, and the band derives the view from
//               the row it is filling.
//   tint        rgb565 modulation, carried and counted unapplied for the same
//               reason (twod_band_tint_dropped_o, twod_tint_unapplied_o).
//   order       composition order. TWOD.SPRITE.md's drop rule and the band's
//               last-write composition both key on it. TIES ARE BROKEN BY
//               COMMAND ORDER, which the ruling requires and which the list's
//               append-only construction gives for free.
//   flags       reserved, MUST be 0.
//   src_id      the sprite's identity: the sampler's binding slot is
//               4 + src_id[1:0], and the band's order_inversion_o uses the
//               change of this field to know one sprite has ended.
//   u, v        fx16 S15.16 UV at the top-left pixel.
//   a00..a11    du/dx, du/dy, dv/dx, dv/dy -- the optional affine. The
//               identity is {1,0,0,1} in fx16.
//
// WHOLE-SPRITE REFUSAL IS PRESERVED (R235). A sprite the band's leaky bucket
// cannot admit is refused BEFORE ONE PIXEL IS RASTERISED and counted on
// twod_band_sprites_refused_budget_o; a list longer than the frame budget drops
// its TAIL and counts on desc_overflow_o. Neither faults the frame.
command DrawSprite 0x0307 implemented {
  i16  x;
  i16  y;
  u16  w;
  u16  h;
  u16  base;          // page-store word address of this sprite's texels
  u8   lstride;       // log2 words per row
  u8   lheight;       // log2 rows
  u8   format;
  u8   palette_id;
  u8   blend;
  u8   view_mask;
  rgb565 tint;
  u8   order;
  u8   flags;         // reserved, must be 0
  u16  src_id;
  pad[2];
  fx16 u;
  fx16 v;
  fx16 a00;           // du/dx
  fx16 a01;           // du/dy
  fx16 a10;           // dv/dx
  fx16 a11;           // dv/dy
}
